public class Solution {
    /**
     * You are given n rectangles represented by a 0-indexed 2D integer array rectangles, where rectangles[i] = [width[i], height[i]] denotes the width and height of the i-th rectangle. Two rectangles i and j (i < j) are considered interchangeable if they have the same width-to-height ratio. More formally, two rectangles are interchangeable if width[i]/height[i] == width[j]/height[j] (using decimal division, not integer division). Return the number of pairs of interchangeable rectangles in rectangles.
     *
     * @param rectangles the 2D integer array representing the rectangles
     * @return the number of pairs of interchangeable rectangles
